From 681e0538f9f0db40f2898d47823e1d5c6d40f0b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:55:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/53] drm/imagination: confine JH7110 platform workarounds

The JH7110 port acquires three extra clocks and a second reset through the
generic img,img-rogue match. Other PowerVR platforms can expose similarly
named resources with unrelated sequencing, and a second reset is not
generically defined by the binding.

Add a StarFive-specific match-data entry and use it to acquire the required
JH7110 resources. Keep all other platforms on their original three-clock,
one-optional-reset path. Rename and document the second reset as the GPU
domain reset, and make both JH7110 resets mandatory.

Also limit the optional Rascal/DUST flag and raw heap-base register writes
to BVNC 36.50.54.182, make the parameter load-time only, and declare the
matching firmware in the module metadata.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
